NAME
    help - list the Y1/OS commands

SYNOPSIS
    help

DESCRIPTION
    Prints one line for each shell built-in and each /BIN program;
    man NAME gives the page for any of them. help is /BIN/HELP.

    The shell also has a built-in help, a four-line summary of the
    built-ins and of < > >> |, used only when /BIN/HELP is missing. `?` always runs
    the built-in one.

EXAMPLES
    help
    ?                    the short built-in summary
    man cd               the page for one command

NOTES
    Removed from the P8X version: the lines for /d1, graphics, kermit,
    make and sh; the built-ins are Y1/OS's; redirection and pipes are
    one line (man shell).
    Ported from P8X os/commands/help.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    man, shell, run, ls
